Option: map-without-traced-land
Name: Farm map without the land traced from the aerial picture
Does: Takes out of js/map-art.js everything the map drew from the farm's aerial picture (Google's): the two roads, the neighbours' houses, the mown lawns, the plowed field and the dirt lanes (the constant SCENERY and the function sceneryFor, and the house drawing only they used). Every mark the farm made stays (parking, entrance, restrooms, strawberries and the rest), and so do the legend, the names, the drive-time chips and the map on the First-visit page. The ground around the marks becomes the forest and the clearings the file already draws by itself. Also: tools/farm_map.py says how to draw the land again from a picture the farm owns (what it writes does not change), the map paragraph of README.md, and row L8 of docs/CREDITS_AND_LICENCES.md (now done).
Answers: d86 (where the map outline of the land came from: option 2, take the traced land out and keep every mark the farm made)
Conflicts: none
Requires: docs/CREDITS_AND_LICENCES.md (the licence list)
Host: any
Order: 70
After: nothing to rebuild; upload again (node tests/run-all.mjs map licences docs)
Strings: none

