index 4a3e874..2ee78d9 100644
--- a/tools/farm_map.py
+++ b/tools/farm_map.py
@@ -13,6 +13,17 @@ What it does
   - rounds the points, keeps them inside the picture, trims very long text
   - writes js/farm-map-data.js (and refuses to overwrite it when the saved map has no usable points)
   - lists any names or notes that still need translating (Spanish, Hindi, Chinese, Vietnamese)
+
+Drawing the land around the farm
+  This tool writes the farm's own marks and nothing else: only "imageSize", "topFaces" and "items" are read from the saved map, so a
+  "scenery" or "source" field in it is ignored. The ground around the marks (forest, clearing, trees, grass) is drawn by js/map-art.js,
+  the same way for every map. No road, neighbour's house, lawn or lane is copied from the picture the points were marked on, and the
+  tool must never write one.
+  To draw the land around the farm from a picture later, the picture must be one the farm owns (its own drone photo, or a plan someone
+  drew for the farm) or one whose licence allows it, such as OpenStreetMap data (it asks for "(c) OpenStreetMap contributors" to be
+  shown with the map); never a Google Earth or Google Maps picture. Mark the map on that picture in
+  the Farm Map Marker, run this tool as above, then ask Claude to add the shapes to the background part of js/map-art.js (in the
+  same units as the points, taken from that picture only) and to write where the picture came from in docs/CREDITS_AND_LICENCES.md.
 """
 import json, math, os, re, sys
 
